WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.090
In 1990, 47 per cent of
people in the developing

2
00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:06.780
world lived in extreme poverty.

3
00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:10.980
By 2015, that share was
down to 14 per cent.

4
00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:13.650
Now the world has set
itself a bigger goal:

5
00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:16.560
to end extreme poverty by 2030,

6
00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.180
not just halve it.

7
00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:20.290
But ending poverty takes growth,

8
00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:22.040
year after year.

9
00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:24.670
So can a country get richer today in a way

10
00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:27.030
that leaves its future poorer?

11
00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:30.790
In this mission, you'll
meet the 17 goals for 2030,

12
00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:34.610
and check real progress on
electricity in three countries.

13
00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:36.530
Then you'll run a forest economy,

14
00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:40.400
decade by decade, and watch
what your choices do to it.

15
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:43.810
Your mission: find out
what makes growth last.
